<title>NEW ZEALAND: National Bank of NZ cuts fixed NZ mortgage rates.</title>
<headline>National Bank of NZ cuts fixed NZ mortgage rates.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of New Zealand said on Thursday it would cut its two year fixed mortgage rate to 8.75 percent from 9.4 percent, and its three year rate to 8.75 percent from 9.5 percent.</p>
<p>The new rates are effective from June 23.</p>
<p>The bank also said it was introducing a five year fixed rate home loan at 8.95 percent, effective from June 25.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734746</p>
